  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Determine the least common multiple of $4,$ $6$ and $8.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's list the multiples of each number. Then, we find the smallest number that appears in all three lists:\n\n- Multiples of $4$: $\\,4,8,12,16,20,24,28…$\n\n- Multiples of $6$: $\\,6,12,18,24,30…$\n\n- Multiples of $8$: $\\,8,16,24,32…$\n\nWe conclude that the least common multiple of  $4,$ $6$ and $8$ is $24.$",
